hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1091","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quti’ and Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam told us, they said: Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, Ibn Juraij told us, H. Muhammad told us Ibn Rafi’, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj, H., Ahmed bin Mansour al-Ramadi told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Sulayman bin Musa also told me, Nafi’ told us, that Ibn Umar used to say: Whoever prays at night, let him make his last prayer string; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that. When dawn comes, all the night prayers and Witr prayers are cancelled. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perform Witr before dawn.” This is the hadith of Al-Quti. The others said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perform Witr before dawn.” Al-Ramadi said: The night prayer and the Witr prayer have disappeared."
"1092","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i, I am Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi, narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawa’i, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Nadra, On the authority of Abu Saeed, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever begins the dawn prayer and does not perform Witr prayer, then there is no Witr prayer for him.”"
